 34S  c  1978Ab02: elastic and inelastic scattering of vector polarized         
 34S 2c  deuterons on 34S. A 11.8-MeV polarized deuteron beam was provided from 
 34S 3c  the University of Wisconsin Lamb-shift polarized ion source and tandem 
 34S 4c  accelerator. The target was 610-ug/cm2 90%-enriched {+34}S on a        
 34S 5c  100-ug/cm2 Au backing. Scattered deuterons were detected using four Si 
 34S 6c  |DE-E telescopes. Measured angular distributions of cross sections     
 34S 7c  |s(E{-d},|q) and angular distributions of vector analyzing powers      
 34S 8c  iT{-11}(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, optical model parameters, and
 34S 9c  vibrational deformation parameters |b{-2} from DWUCK-DWBA and CHUCK    
 34S Ac  coupled-channels analysis.                                             
 34S  c  1987Nu01: elastic and inelastic scattering of vector polarized         
 34S 2c  deuterons on a series of nuclei including 34S. A 52-MeV polarized      
 34S 3c  deuteron beam was provided from the Lamb-shift polarized ion source and
 34S 4c  the Karlsruhe isochronous cyclotron. The target was 89.8%-enriched     
 34S 5c  {+34}SH{-2}. Scattered deuterons were detected using six |DE-E         
 34S 6c  solid-state counter telescopes. Measured angular distributions of cross
 34S 7c  sections |s(E{-d},|q) and angular distributions of vector analyzing    
 34S 8c  powers iT{-11}(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, optical model         
 34S 9c  parameters, and vibrational deformation parameters |b{-2} from DWBA and
 34S Ac  coupled-channels analysis.                                             
 34S  c  Other: 34S(pol d,d) elastic scattering (1975Ba29).                     
